{"audit_run_id":"audit:198f7e44434e4cb7a0da9b7f30134396","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":86,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"`damselfly_condition.csv` — 70 data rows plus one header row, comma separated, UTF-8."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"One row is one adult male blue-tailed damselfly. Each insect was hand-netted within two days of"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"emergence, at a single pond, and measured individually in the laboratory on the day of capture. No"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"insect appears twice, and every insect has a value in every column, so there are no missing cells."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"Seventy insects are present: 35 netted at fish-free ponds and 35 netted at fish-stocked ponds. All"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"ponds lie in one lowland landscape and were sampled in the same fortnight. Specimen serial numbers"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"run in capture order, which interleaves the two pond types, so the serial number does not track the"},{"end_column":11,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"pond type."},{"end_column":45,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| Column | Type | Units / values | Meaning |"},{"end_column":26,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":147,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `specimen_id` | text | `dam_001` … `dam_070` | Unique specimen identifier: the prefix `dam` plus a zero-padded serial number in capture order. |"},{"end_column":192,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `pond_type` | text | exactly two values: `fish_free`, `fish` | Group column. The type of pond the insect emerged from: `fish_free` = pond holding no fish, `fish` = pond stocked with fish. |"},{"end_column":127,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `body_length_mm` | number | millimetres, 0.1 mm | Total body length, head to abdomen tip, measured with digital callipers. |"},{"end_column":109,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `hindwing_length_mm` | number | millimetres, 0.1 mm | Hind-wing length, measured with digital callipers. |"},{"end_column":150,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `abdominal_fat_mg` | number | milligrams, 0.01 mg | Abdominal fat content, dry mass of the solvent-extracted fat body, weighed on a microbalance. |"},{"end_column":160,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `mite_count` | integer | whole mites, count | Ectoparasitic water-mite load: number of mites attached to the individual, counted under a stereo microscope. |"},{"end_column":230,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `encapsulation_grey` | integer | greyscale value, 0–255 | Immune encapsulation response to a nylon monofilament implant, read as an 8-bit greyscale darkness value. Higher values mean a darker, stronger encapsulation response. |"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"The five outcome columns appear in the order fixed by the field protocol before sampling:"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"body length, hind-wing length, abdominal fat, mite load, encapsulation response."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"The values are fixed and committed in the CSV. They were produced once by `make_data.py`, which"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"draws each outcome from the distributions stated in the field protocol, keeps the within-individual"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"correlations that real morphometric and condition measures show, and rounds every value to the"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"precision of the stated measurement method. The generator is kept for reference only; the analysis"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"reads the CSV."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:912be9bfdfd2c9a6cff1","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:f02478aa42d793ba94de5c43069726eb27c167bc81118f0de5fc7ef4cca22c91","end_line":39,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-39","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:198f7e44434e4cb7a0da9b7f30134396","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":100,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `pond_type` column of `damselfly_condition.csv`."},{"end_column":144,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: body_length_mm, hindwing_length_mm, abdominal_fat_mg, mite_count, encapsulation_grey."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:6f27dfe206296af73e06","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:c740474403f860ef82d627282f90761a973fc19cf4ebdc674260366ee3f37584","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
