{"audit_run_id":"audit:198f7e44434e4cb7a0da9b7f30134396","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":87,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Does the presence of fish in a pond go with a difference in the condition of the adult"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"damselflies that emerge from it? Seventy adult male blue-tailed damselflies were hand-netted"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"within two days of emergence: 35 at fish-free ponds (ponds holding no fish) and 35 at"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"fish-stocked ponds. All ponds lie in one lowland landscape and were sampled in the same"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"fortnight. The two pond types are the only comparison in the study. Each damselfly is one"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"subject, measured individually in the laboratory on the day of capture."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"File: `damselfly_condition.csv`, 70 data rows and one header row. **One row is one adult male"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"damselfly.** No insect appears twice, and every insect has a value in every column, so there are"},{"end_column":18,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"no missing cells."},{"end_column":9,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"Columns:"},{"end_column":21,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| Column | Meaning |"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| --- | --- |"},{"end_column":112,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `specimen_id` | Unique specimen identifier, prefix `dam` plus a zero-padded serial number in capture order. |"},{"end_column":124,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `pond_type` | Group column, exactly two values: `fish_free` (pond holding no fish) and `fish` (pond stocked with fish). |"},{"end_column":84,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `body_length_mm` | Total body length in millimetres, digital callipers, 0.1 mm. |"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `hindwing_length_mm` | Hind-wing length in millimetres, digital callipers, 0.1 mm. |"},{"end_column":107,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `abdominal_fat_mg` | Abdominal fat content in milligrams, dry mass of the extracted fat body, 0.01 mg. |"},{"end_column":89,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `mite_count` | Ectoparasitic water-mite load, whole mites counted on the individual. |"},{"end_column":147,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `encapsulation_grey` | Immune encapsulation response to a nylon implant, 8-bit greyscale darkness value, 0-255. Higher is a stronger response. |"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"The five outcome columns appear in the order fixed by the field protocol before sampling:"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"body length, hind-wing length, abdominal fat, mite load, encapsulation response."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"The five outcomes were declared in the field protocol as **one outcome family**, so the error"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"rate is controlled across the complete family rather than outcome by outcome."},{"end_column":92,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"Each outcome was compared between the two pond types with a two-sample t-test, and the five"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"p-values were kept together in the declared order. All five were then adjusted in a single call,"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"as one complete family, with the Holm step-down method from **pingouin** (`pingouin.multicomp`,"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"version 0.5.5), a specialist Python statistics package used here for the multiple-comparison"},{"end_column":69,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"correction. Holm gives strong control of the family-wise error rate."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"Every verdict below was read only from the adjusted p-value, at the conventional 0.05 threshold."},{"end_column":84,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"No outcome was called from an unadjusted p-value. The analysis is in `analysis.py`."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"In the declared order (means are group means; p is the family-adjusted p-value):"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"1. **Total body length (mm).** Fish-free 30.186, fish 29.574. Adjusted p = 0.0789."},{"end_column":24,"end_line":52,"start_column":4,"start_line":52,"text":"**Not significant.**"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"2. **Hind-wing length (mm).** Fish-free 16.714, fish 16.334. Adjusted p = 0.0750."},{"end_column":24,"end_line":54,"start_column":4,"start_line":54,"text":"**Not significant.**"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"3. **Abdominal fat (mg).** Fish-free 1.413, fish 1.062. Adjusted p = 0.0002."},{"end_column":20,"end_line":56,"start_column":4,"start_line":56,"text":"**Significant.**"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":57,"start_column":1,"start_line":57,"text":"4. **Water-mite load (mites).** Fish-free 2.914, fish 4.514. Adjusted p = 0.0104."},{"end_column":20,"end_line":58,"start_column":4,"start_line":58,"text":"**Significant.**"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"5. **Encapsulation response (greyscale).** Fish-free 130.600, fish 114.629. Adjusted p = 0.0283."},{"end_column":20,"end_line":60,"start_column":4,"start_line":60,"text":"**Significant.**"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"Hind-wing length had an unadjusted p of 0.0375, which would have cleared 0.05 on its own, but it"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":63,"start_column":1,"start_line":63,"text":"does not clear the threshold once the complete family of five is accounted for, so it is reported"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":64,"start_column":1,"start_line":64,"text":"as not significant."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"Adults emerging from fish-stocked ponds carried less abdominal fat, more ectoparasitic water"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"mites, and mounted a weaker immune encapsulation response than adults from fish-free ponds."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":70,"start_column":1,"start_line":70,"text":"The two size measures, body length and hind-wing length, ran in the same direction but did not"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":71,"start_column":1,"start_line":71,"text":"separate the groups once the whole declared family was corrected together. Fish presence in the"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"larval pond is therefore associated with poorer adult condition in the energetic, parasite, and"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"immune measures, while overall adult size looks much the same. This is an observational field"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"comparison of ponds, not an experiment, so it shows an association and does not establish that"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"fish cause the difference."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:182f914522e167cec812","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:ee6cddcb919aa03a6a4acdabf2eb8248c730a8de33c587def0df1ff41778e99e","end_line":75,"locator":"report.md:1-75","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
